{
  "dom_id": "questionExplanation-314885",
  "name": null,
  "problem": "",
  "worked_solution": "We use the central difference approximation\n\n$$\n{f}^{′}(x)≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h}\n$$\n\n \nat the point $x=2$ with the step size $h=0.1.$ This gives\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{f}^{′}(x) & ≈\\frac{f(x+h)-f(x-h)}{2h} \\\\ {f}^{′}(2) & ≈\\frac{f(2+0.1)-f(2-0.1)}{2(0.1)} \\\\  & =\\frac{f(2.1)-f(1.9)}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{5.81-4.21}{0.2} \\\\  & =\\frac{1.6}{0.2} \\\\  & =8.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
  "calculator_instructions": "",
  "fields": [],
  "problem_field_keys": [],
  "answer_fields_complete": null,
  "result": null,
  "proof_feedback": null,
